# Needed so Waypointer can construct custom RenderTypes and smooth HUD labels.
# Three things are widened:
#
#   RenderType.create(String, RenderSetup) -- package-private in vanilla; this
#     is the only constructor for a RenderType that wraps an arbitrary
#     RenderPipeline, which we need so our pipeline (depth test disabled) can
#     actually be drawn through a MultiBufferSource.
#
#   RenderPipelines.LINES_SNIPPET -- private static Snippet that vanilla uses
#     as the shared base for LINES and LINES_TRANSLUCENT. Building from the
#     snippet is the only way to inherit the line shader + vertex format
#     without hard-coding shader identifiers that Mojang may rename.
#
#   GameRenderer.getFov(Camera, float, boolean) -- vanilla's public
#     projectPointToScreen hardcodes tickProgress=0, which makes HUD-projected
#     waypoint labels step during sprint FOV transitions. Calling getFov with
#     the camera partial tick lets labels match the world's smooth projection.
